{
  "id": "Compound::DB06738 - Gene::1559",
  "verbalization": "Ketobemidone is shown to bind to Cyp2c8 and Cyp3a4, both of which are involved in oxidoreductive activities that involve quinone or similar compound acceptors. These activities are central to the metabolism of various substrates, and Cyp2c9 is a known participant in these pathways. The evidence suggests that Ketobemidone may influence Cyp2c9 through its interaction with Cyp2c8, which in turn participates in the same metabolic processes as Cyp2c9. This creates a potential mechanism by which Ketobemidone could modulate Cyp2c9 activity, possibly affecting the metabolism of substrates that are oxidized by this enzyme. The shared involvement in similar metabolic pathways supports a mechanistic link between Ketobemidone and Cyp2c9, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated. The evidence is consistent with a role for Ketobemidone in modulating Cyp2c9 activity through its interaction with Cyp2c8, but further experimental validation is needed to confirm this relationship.",
